#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Matrix of Cofactors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d0b4dc5-34b5-5f8d-a240-32f407402e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350236} {:answer/id #uuid "1c004200-c624-5ed8-afc6-04b2522df8f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350237} {:answer/id #uuid "9b15630c-0939-5999-9d68-ae09bdd16144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350238} {:answer/id #uuid "d620ffac-9077-5a93-8b15-d2838786a131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350239} {:answer/id #uuid "ba465286-cacf-5d3a-9dbd-d03815a6a7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d620ffac-9077-5a93-8b15-d2838786a131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350239} :answer-field/id #uuid "3088c17f-4733-53b9-ab9d-7bb976aa64c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103533" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fbb3d41-56e7-5eae-90a8-573f9ed56c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350243} {:answer/id #uuid "8150fcc4-dff1-5d98-81d5-08e1d4c2a98b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350244} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd3a52-d7d9-5dc0-aa01-6c25c171c46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350245} {:answer/id #uuid "3a13a970-f1ca-5977-9640-6b2ef1d621d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350246} {:answer/id #uuid "f1100339-16cb-5378-b2f7-e2c7a8b3f367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd3a52-d7d9-5dc0-aa01-6c25c171c46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350245} :answer-field/id #uuid "f422f321-aec1-5295-860e-00912f1578f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b521d3e-8961-5736-a1f0-287985c900e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-18287" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $24.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =24-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot 24=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cofactor Method To Solve for an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3262839-4028-5d90-bf8a-cb4de958813a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279523} {:answer/id #uuid "0e326d50-6309-5e63-ba00-a5eb1f4e96b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e326d50-6309-5e63-ba00-a5eb1f4e96b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279524} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d153166-8679-52de-a7b3-11c4606fe3fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39eba7b4-55f1-5b6e-bfe4-784dcc986294" :question/math-academy-id "q-319437" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaf02b36-d0d0-5f73-80e4-310c5dc697f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaf02b36-d0d0-5f73-80e4-310c5dc697f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350250} :answer-field/id #uuid "45cb5e56-e7f3-5703-b61e-344ab9484e6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6721d39e-b612-5be9-97a4-8835ad206e75" :question/math-academy-id "q-319546" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cofactor Method To Solve for an Unknown Quantity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b92df9bf-57f8-52c4-bdb1-778f42842a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288574} {:answer/id #uuid "30d4d4f3-edf3-50e0-b558-676c2c519051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288575} {:answer/id #uuid "88d0c1ad-2e69-53e8-b0f1-14231d6b6c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288576} {:answer/id #uuid "104c5573-009e-55dc-872f-3406140f4ce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288577} {:answer/id #uuid "42c0d506-1aa1-50f1-925f-3776c434998d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d4d4f3-edf3-50e0-b558-676c2c519051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288575} :answer-field/id #uuid "32185872-743f-5625-abaf-14cc3904b386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b53bfca7-a35b-5bdd-8a26-779771b1f95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9980" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
